cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Quantum Nematode: a closed-loop brain-architecture comparison platform on the C. elegans connectome"
authors:
  - family-names: Zaharia
    given-names: Chris Julian
repository-code: "https://github.com/SyntheticBrains/nematode"
url: "https://github.com/SyntheticBrains/nematode"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.5.0
date-released: "2026-08-23"
keywords:
  - C. elegans
  - connectome
  - computational neuroscience
  - reinforcement learning
  - embodied learning
  - evolutionary optimisation
  - quantum machine learning
  - simulation
abstract: >-
  A closed-loop sensory-motor simulation platform in which a simulated nematode
  forages, evades predators and navigates thermal and oxygen gradients while a
  pluggable brain architecture — feed-forward, recurrent, spiking, reservoir,
  quantum, hybrid, GA-evolved or constrained to the real 302-neuron C. elegans
  connectome — is trained by learning or evolution. Architectures are ranked on
  the same behaviours under a paired-seed statistical protocol, and the learned
  behaviour is validated against published C. elegans behavioural data.
